TITLE: Final Report

FastAPI is a Python class that provides the core functionality for building APIs. It inherits directly from [Starlette](https://www.starlette.dev/), meaning you can utilize all Starlette features while using FastAPI.

### What is it used for?
FastAPI is primarily used to create and manage web APIs. Its main features and use cases include:

*   **API Development:** It serves as the main point of interaction for defining your API, including creating "path operations" (also known as endpoints or routes) to separate different resources and concerns.
*   **Application Deployment:** You can use the `fastapi` command-line interface to run your application. For example:
    *   `fastapi dev`: Used for development, it enables "auto-reload" so the server updates automatically when you change your code.
    *   `fastapi run`: Used for production, it disables auto-reload and listens on all available IP addresses (`0.0.0.0`), which is typically how applications are run in containers.
*   **Automatic Documentation:** When running your application, FastAPI provides automatic API documentation (accessible at `/docs`), which helps visualize your paths, tags, and endpoints.

For more technical details, you can refer to the documentation files in the repository, such as `docs/en/docs/tutorial/first-steps.md` and `docs/zh/docs/fastapi-cli.md`.

